From: Kirill =?UTF-8?q?M=C3=BCller?= <kirill@cynkra.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Accept a lower-case drive letter in Windows paths

LocalFileSystem::PathStartsWithDrive() accepts only 'A' to 'Z', so a path
spelled with a lower-case drive letter is not recognised as one. The
effect shows in CanonicalizePath(), which walks up from the full path to
the longest prefix that exists and turns a bare drive into its root on
the way. For c:/missing/db.duckdb, where nothing below the root exists,
the walk arrives at "c:", leaves it as it stands, and asks Windows to
resolve it. "c:" is drive-relative, so it resolves to the current
directory on that drive, and the path comes back as
<current directory>\missing\db.duckdb. A database opened with a
lower-case drive letter in a directory that does not exist yet is
thereby created somewhere else, or reported missing under a name the
caller never gave; the upper-case spelling of the same path is right.

The check now uses StringUtil::CharacterIsAlpha(), as Path's own drive
parsing does. MakePathAbsolute() compared the drive of a drive-relative
path (c:db.duckdb) with the working directory's case-sensitively, which
the first change makes reachable for a lower-case letter: it now
compares them upper-cased, so a drive-relative path on the current
drive resolves against the working directory whichever case either is
spelled in.

duckdb-r reaches this through the driver cache, which keys a database
on LocalFileSystem::CanonicalizePath() and opens the path it returns
(handbook/usage/connections/README.md).

main and v2.0-cyanoptera do not need this: their MakePathAbsolute()
goes through Path, which upper-cases the drive letter before the walk
starts. The first hunk still applies there and the second does not, so
a series vendored from either leaves this entry out rather than
rebasing it.

Proposed upstream in duckdb/duckdb#<PR> (placeholder: not opened yet)
against v1.5-variegata, and carried here until a release carries it.
---
 src/duckdb/src/common/local_file_system.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/common/local_file_system.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/common/local_file_system.cpp
index 3fd4266371..73f36c391c 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/common/local_file_system.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/common/local_file_system.cpp
@@ -1398,7 +1398,7 @@ bool LocalFileSystem::TryCanonicalizeExistingPath(string &input) {
 }
 
 bool LocalFileSystem::PathStartsWithDrive(const string &path) {
-	return path.size() >= 2 && path[0] >= 'A' && path[0] <= 'Z' && path[1] == ':';
+	return path.size() >= 2 && StringUtil::CharacterIsAlpha(path[0]) && path[1] == ':';
 }
 
 bool LocalFileSystem::IsPathAbsolute(const string &path) {
@@ -1429,7 +1429,7 @@ string LocalFileSystem::MakePathAbsolute(const string &path_p, optional_ptr<File
 		}
 		// this is "C:" - expand to current working directory if this is the current drive
 		auto working_directory = GetWorkingDirectory();
-		if (working_directory[0] != path[0]) {
+		if (StringUtil::CharacterToUpper(working_directory[0]) != StringUtil::CharacterToUpper(path[0])) {
 			// this is not the drive we are on right now (e.g. referencing D: while in C:)
 			// default to root of drive
 			working_directory = string(1, path[0]) + ":\\";
